  "mcp" : null,
  "mcp_requires_auth" : false,
  "output" : "Yes to both — but the mechanics differ. Here's what I verified empirically on your install (v2.1.289):\n\n## MCP: use `--mcp-config`\n\n```bash\nclaude --bare --mcp-config ./mcp.json\n# or inline JSON, and multiple sources:\nclaude --bare --mcp-config '{\"mcpServers\":{\"fs\":{\"command\":\"npx\",\"args\":[\"-y\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\",\"/tmp\"]}}}'\n```\n\n- Format is the standard `{\"mcpServers\": {...}}` with stdio/http/sse entries.\n- **Without** this flag, bare mode loads *zero* MCP servers — your usual `.mcp.json` and user-configured servers are skipped (confirmed: a bare run with no flag saw no servers). So `--strict-mcp-config` is effectively already implied in bare mode.\n- What does **not** work in bare mode (tested): `--settings '{\"mcpServers\": ...}'`, plugin-bundled MCP via `--plugin-dir` (both in `plugin.json` manifest and `.mcp.json` form).\n\n## Skills: discovered, but only load on-demand via `/name`\n\nThis is the subtle one. In bare mode, skills are **not advertised** in the system prompt (the model will tell you it has \"no skills\"), but they **are still resolvable** when explicitly invoked with slash syntax — exactly as the `--bare` help text says (\"Skills still resolve via `/skill-name`\"). Verified working sources:\n\n1. **Project skills**: `<cwd>/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` → invoke as `/name`\n2. **Via plugin**: `--plugin-dir /path/to/plugin` with `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` → invoke as `/name`\n\nSo a complete bare invocation looks like:\n\n```bash\nclaude --bare \\\n  --mcp-config ./mcp.json \\\n  --plugin-dir ./my-plugin \\\n  -p \"/my-skill do the thing\"\n```\n\nCaveats worth knowing:\n- Since skills aren't in the prompt, the model won't *autonomously* decide to use them based on descriptions — you have to name them, or reference them in your prompt/system prompt (`--append-system-prompt`) so the model knows to call them.\n- Note that bare mode also skips `CLAUDE.md` auto-discovery; `--add-dir` is the escape hatch if you need dirs with CLAUDE.md context.\n\nAlso, unrelated heads-up: your environment routes through `api.z.ai` with a GLM model — that works fine in bare mode (env-based auth survives), just be aware tool availability there may differ from Anthropic defaults.\n"
}
